NAME
       ip - show and change network interfaces, addresses and routes

SYNOPSIS
       **ip** **a**[ddr] [**show**]
       **ip** **addr add** __A.B.C.D/N__ **dev** __NAME__
       **ip** **addr flush** **dev** __NAME__
       **ip** **link**
       **ip** **route** [**show**]
       **ip** **route add** **default via** __GATEWAY__ **dev** __NAME__
       **ip** **route del** **default dev** __NAME__
       **ip** **dns set** __A.B.C.D__ **dev** __NAME__
       **ip** **dhcp start**|**stop** **dev** __NAME__

DESCRIPTION
       Show the state of network interfaces and change their IPv4
       configuration. Changes need root or the NET_ADMIN capability; showing
       is allowed for everyone.

       The loopback interface **lo** always has 127.0.0.1/8 and cannot be
       removed.

       **ip dns** and **ip dhcp** are PureC OS extensions: they set the DNS
       server of an interface and start or stop the kernel DHCP client.

EXAMPLES
       ip a
       ip addr add 192.168.0.50/24 dev eth0
       ip route add default via 192.168.0.1 dev eth0
       ip dns set 1.1.1.1 dev eth0
       ip dhcp start dev eth0

SEE ALSO
       ping(1), services(5)
